{"title":"Subjectwise Test-12 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 CS Discrete Mathematics","fileName":"031_Subjectwise Test-12 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 CS Discrete Mathematics.html","branch":"COMPUTER SCIENCE ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 GATE 2025 Online Test Series Computer Science Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":5400,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider three finite set <em>A</em>, <em>B</em> and <em>C</em> :</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/c7098627f843eae070de59d3f75a1b57dfebc9da.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Sets <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> are related as</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/0cd7ebbe86a08928c1029bb371ee213ddd17b29a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/4a27bfa709927f71d94f77fe54cbf06060fe555b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/abcd62f53492e09945f8044c8cac1b314f9f6e4b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/fdd955146dae08f771784c8a67b7680ee4f9487a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n A fair coin is tossed three times in succession. If the first toss produces a head, then what is the probability of getting exactly two heads in three tosses?</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.5","high":"0.5"},"solution":"<p>\n 0.5</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/3b1909452a7a33d13e99f9f58763c8761d227245.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Let a graph (<em>G</em>) has 4 vertices and there are 2 vertices are of degree 2, 1 vertices of degree 1 and remaining vertex of degree 3. Then complement of <em>G</em> is ________.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Connected</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Disconnected</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Either (a) or (b)</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/bd5b679f2852f2844964b194544537e9605fa778.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the following graphs:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/39520c6830a18107e726931dfbdae571fd7d2a36.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Identity the correct statements?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n Only G<sub>1</sub> is Hamiltonian</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n Only G<sub>2</sub> is Hamiltonian</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n Both G<sub>1</sub> and G<sub>2</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n Neither G<sub>1</sub> nor G<sub>2</sub> is Hamiltonian</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/377624f7f84fb5cb3f29df37b768ae0731b4a066.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":5,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the following statements is/are true?<br />\n <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : In a lattice every two elements need not have both join and meet.<br />\n <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : In a distributive lattice L, a given element can have atmost one complement.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n Only <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n Only <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n Both <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Neither of them</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)<br />\n <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> is false because poset would be called as lattice iff any two elements must have both meet and join.<br />\n <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> is true because if any element has complement then it must be unique.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Identify the contrapositive for the following statement. “If a real number is greater than 2, then its square is greater than 4”.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/0e7ee3d077f1c0b1b4d20d2dca24789957dd89cd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/acf158e39f46acb6b1927a110cff90ed90491dc3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/1dc07ff136056f9c40736334277a110ab6671398.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/05deacfc484c4411985bfd0c525614e750af670b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider a relation <img src=\"/media/25b80ba0dd76d25098fd5df0f02e67154e8f4900.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> on positive integers ≤ 4. Which of the following is true?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>R</em> is reflexive, symmetric and transitive.</p>\n</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>R</em> is symmetric and transitive.</p>\n</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>R</em> is antisymmetric and transitive.</p>\n</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>R</em> is symmetric.</p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/75fb455e88c8447f10bb0787052199f93b3b0675.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Let G be a graph with 25 vertices and 40 edges. G contain all vertices that have degree 2, 3 or 4.<br />\n If G has exactly 4 vertices of degree 2, then the number of vertices of degree 4 does G contain are _________.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"9","high":"9"},"solution":"<p>\n 9</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/97c1d251b5e0058a6728c09737bb3bd64073af5e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,C,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider set <em>S</em> = {10, 20, 30, 41, 52, 59, 60}. Which of the following is/are the correct partition of the given set?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> {{10}, {20}, {30, 41}, {52, 59, 60}}</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> {{10}, {10, 20, 30, 41}, {52, 59, 60}}</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> {{10}, {20}, {30}, {41}, {52}, {59}, {60}}</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> {{10, 20}, {30, 41}, {52}, {59, 60}}</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a, c, d)<br />\n A partition of a set <em>S</em> is a collection of disjoint non-empty subsets of <em>S</em> that have <em>S</em> as their union. For partition in (b) {10} and {10, 20, 30, 41} are not disjoint and hence is not correct partition.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n The number of ways to distribute 6 different gifts to 2 student from total 4 students are ________.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"384","high":"384"},"solution":"<p>\n 384</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/24ddb26f32aca58103812271e1d47791c6c17a5d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n The numbers [Each with different digits] between 1000 and 10000 can be formed with 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2 are _________ .</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"360","high":"360"},"solution":"<p>\n 360</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/647ea815f69ecc5ff392193a7e01190caee4aa0e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the following lattice:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/477bbdd190076517e1c546f4dfa43cf3e56177df.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The number of complements of <em>h</em> are __________ .</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"5","high":"5"},"solution":"<p>\n 5</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/d8a4e05ec66ea3f935bf6cc730b08596681a9497.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Match <strong>List-I</strong> and <strong>List-II</strong> and select the correct answer using the codes given below the lists:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/3a50f6003548c006f1ea458c2b4b36db26cc992a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> a</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> b</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> c</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> d</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/31949847b3f50974947fb644d6974eb8a210198e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the following statements :<br />\n <em>S</em><sub>1</sub>: The maximum number of edges in a disconnected simple graph having two components and n-vertices is <img src=\"/media/a528b56f44c25e7237ff1ba2ec3fa5cc252270df.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <em>S</em><sub>2</sub>: A simple graph G (with n-vertices and k-components) is a forest if and only if <em>G</em> has (<em>n</em> – <em>k</em>) edges.<br />\n Find which of the above statements are correct</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> only</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> only</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n Both <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n Neither <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> nor <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/8b9dc27a5e3b577fcb801655dc027497baf9c591.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":15,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the following graph:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/66abfc93d9fb9e7cf24cd534977e8d19d52705a4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n How many edges are present in complementary graph <img src=\"/media/4f4fa0a92852705b458766e41470d96f89db6a2c.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> of the given graph G?</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"3","high":"3"},"solution":"<p>\n 3</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/f86591bb32c2592746391e2e54ef5f78f32fabd5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/c03a0e0366e23d9cfecff2dbbd87913d2e1761c2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":16,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider of the following is/are valid:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/20e53569d36647e5550870830fb5d1cfb8d69227.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 1 and 2</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 2 and 3</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 1 and 3</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 1, 2 and 3</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)<br />\n 1. is valid by constructive dilemma.<br />\n 2. is valid by disjunctive dilemma.<br />\n 3. hypothetical syllogious.<br />\n All of the above are known rules of inference.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":17,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n A binary relation <em>R</em> on Z × Z is defined as follows:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/0a1e0681d086abf1d8456132da4fd7e11535bb3c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Consider the following propositions:<br />\n 1. <em>R</em> is reflexive.<br />\n 2. <em>R</em> is symmetric.<br />\n 3. <em>R</em> is antisymmetric.<br />\n Which one of the following statements is True?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Both 1 and 2 are true</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 1 is true and 2 is false</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 1 is false and 3 is true</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Both 2 and 3 are true</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/5c2b5a8995a4150d105da220a19af6a75036b82b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":18,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Which recurrence relation satisfy the sequence: 2, 3, 4, ..., for n ≥ 1.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/ec49db5602bb77d9c02f01827bcd1064bf22e07a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/2f34c17bd7078b8e8e37212ae58fba87f0f1756f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/d3410dca9c3645a1376b02b9c2a185c06554f6eb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/0c0dc1812f74a2ed49210b940ff1ff6817a690f2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":19,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider statements:<br />\n <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : A finite lattice is always bounded.<br />\n <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : Complemented lattice is a proper subset of bounded lattice.<br />\n <em>S</em><sub>3</sub> : A bounded and complemented lattice may or may not be a distributive lattice.<br />\n Which of the following is/are true?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>3</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>3</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>S</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>3</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)<br />\n &bull; A lattice is bounded iff the lattice has a greatest and a least element.<br />\n &there4; A finite lattice is always bounded.<br />\n &bull; Complemented lattice is defined only for bounded lattice. A bounded lattice is complemented iff atleast one complement of every element exist in lattice. An element should one or more complements.<br />\n &bull; A complemented lattice is distributive iff every element has a unique complement.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":20,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the following lattice:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/f44cb33e9fc1894f0e7e9fd93ee868d2003e1e63.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n How many number of complements for the element ‘<em>b</em>’?</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"1","high":"1"},"solution":"<p>\n 1</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/8b5c2d728d13c046d29907bcffc86f8f19f2b5bb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":21,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the following statement is correct?<br />\n <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : Cycle graph with n vertices has n – 1 spanning tree with <em>n</em> > 2.<br />\n <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : k-regular graph with total n vertices contain <img src=\"/media/def2c102286848576492e4a2d7c66b914fb43bc2.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> edges.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Only (i)</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Only (ii)</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Both (i) and (ii)</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Neither (i) nor (ii)</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/8a59fa5b2e6c9966aa0b8e2bc9030a3030a245d3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":22,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the following statements:<br />\n <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : Every cyclic group is Abelian group.<br />\n <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : Every Abelian group is cyclic group.<br />\n <em>S</em><sub>3</sub> : Cyclic group of order 10 have 4 generators.<br />\n Which of the following is true?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> only</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>3</sub> only</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>3</sub> only</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>S</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>3</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/9d0f893cdd1153a3a68607fca0e140bb77a3ded2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":23,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,B,C","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the following is/are false?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Set of integers on addition operation is Monoid but not group.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Set of integers on subtraction operation is Monoid but not group.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Set of integers on multiplication operation is group but not Abelian group.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a, b, c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/dc03844f2783fbeec2d994cd5e04f16b58b9a31d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":24,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the following statements are equivalent for graph with atleast 1 edge?<br />\n 1. <em>G</em> is bipartite<br />\n 2. A graph <em>G</em> is 2 colourable<br />\n 3. Graph <em>G</em> has a Hamiltonian circuit<br />\n 4. Every cycle of <em>G</em> is of even length</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 1 and 3</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 1, 2 and 3</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 1, 2 and 4</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 3 and 4</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/3921c664f84693546dcc7d4381458af20000c160.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":25,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the following graph:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/8c9b177b5d4bdf9a9f371ac5269ba4e445981027.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Consider the following statements:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/53a96cadab99dde3f69f2f6044b332892ec4490f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Which of the following is correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n Only <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> is correct</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n Only <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> is correct</p></div>"